0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, APRIL 5, 2006\r\rMayor Washburn called the meeting to order at 7:05 p.m. in Conference Room No. 2, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Washburn, Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, Councilmembers Maurer, Wolfson.\r Absent: Councilmember Groveman.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles.\r\rCLOSED SESSION\r\rThe City Council recessed at 7:06 p.m. into closed session to confer with legal counsel regarding the following:\r\r1. \u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015Real property negotiations, pursuant to Government Code Section 54956.8\r Agency Negotiator: Maureen Tamuri, Community Development Director\r Negotiating parties: City of Calabasas and Spotlight the Arts\r Instruction: Discussion regarding Memorandum of Understanding Terms \r Identity of property: Assessor�s Parcel Numbers 2068-003-900 & 2068-003-901\r\r2. Real property negotiations, pursuant to Government Code Section 54956.8\r Agency Negotiator: Maureen Tamuri, Community Development Director\r Negotiating parties: City of Calabasas and Cypress Calabasas LLC; \rCity of Calabasas and Annalisa Maddy\r Instruction: Discussion regarding drafting Letters of Intent to Vacate \r Identity of property: Assessor�s Parcel Number 2064-004-021; \r26787 Agoura Road (APN 2064-021-001)\r\rThe City Council reconvened at 7:34 p.m. from closed session and Mayor Groveman called the meeting to order at 7:44 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Washburn, Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, Councilmembers Groveman (arrived at 8:25 p.m.), Maurer, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Lysik, Peirce, Rubin, Tamuri, Yalda.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Alex DeJesse.\r\rMichael G. Colantuono, City Attorney, stated that the Council provided direction to staff but did not take any action which required reporting. \r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\r Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Councilmember Groveman was absent.\r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\rMayor Washburn presented a cake in recognition of the City�s 15th Year Anniversary of cityhood. Mayor Washburn and Mayor pro Tem Bozajian presented a proclamation to Stephen Pfahler in recognition of his appointment as a Los Angeles Superior Court Judge by Governor Schwarzenegger. Mayor Washburn announced an upcoming art exhibit on April 9, 2006 for the Mountains Restoration Trust at Headwaters Corners. He spoke regarding �Seniors Workshop� at the Calabasas/Agoura Hills Community Center that he attended on April 4, 2006. He announced events during the upcoming week for the MethodFest Film Festival.\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r Michael Brockman, Calabasas, spoke regarding problems with mail delivery and poor service with the United States Postal Service. Keith Zajic, Calabasas, stressed the importance of the Mulholland Highway Beautification Project and the prioritization of and allocation of additional funds to street paving projects and spoke in opposition to private recreational use of A.C. Stelle. Mary Ellen Waller, Calabasas, spoke in opposition to overcrowded street parking in the City of Calabasas.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r\r Approval of the minutes for the March 1, 2006 City Council meeting.\r\r Approval of the minutes for the March 15, 2006 City Council meeting.\r\r Recommendation to renew the facility use agreement with Tri Valley Roller Hockey at Juan Bautista de Anza Park.\r\r Award of professional services agreement for as-needed specialty inspection and testing services to Twinings Laboratories of Southern California.\r\r Recommendation to approve the reappointment of Robert Hill by Mayor pro Tempore Bozajian and Britt Aaronson by Councilmember Maurer to the Library Commission, term ending March 31, 2009.\r\r Recommendation to approve the appointment of Michael Friedman by Councilmember Washburn to the Environmental Commission, term ending March 31, 2007.\r\r Recommendation to�purchase an automated�playback�system for CTV�for tapeless playback and video archiving from Media Control Systems (LLC) in an amount not to exceed $28,591.\r\r Approval of the creation of a full-time permanent Deputy City Engineer position.\r\r Approval of the creation of a full-time permanent Senior Management Analyst position.\r\r An amendment to an existing Professional Services Agreement for as-needed professional planning services to Joyce Parker Bozylinski.\r\r Recommendation to approve an assignment and assumption of lease and consent with Amirian Family Trust.\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson \u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer, to approve Consent Items #1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 8, 9, 10, 11. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Councilmember Groveman was absent.\r\rFollowing some discussion, Councilmember Wolfson \u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, to approve Consent Item #7. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Councilmember Groveman was absent.\r\rFollowing the introduction of Michael Friedman, Councilmember Maurer \u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to approve Consent Item #6. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT (CONTINUED)\r\r Don Wallace, unincorporated Calabasas, Karyne Ventris, Agoura Hills, Steve Hess, Agoura Hills, Michael Brockman, Calabasas, Arthur Carvalho, unincorporated Calabasas, Ted Depass, Calabasas, Ruth Gerson, spoke in support of approving a pending permit for equestrian use of a property located on Las Virgenes Road. Stephanie Abronson, Monte Nido, spoke in support of the City Council adopting the Los Angeles County Zoning Code section which allows for 8 horses per acre rather than the City�s allowance for 2 horses per acre. Kathryn Palmer, Calabasas, expressed concern over speeding cars on Cold Springs Street and spoke regarding poor customer service she received at the Lost Hills Sheriff�s Station. Earlyn Mosher, Calabasas, invited the community to an upcoming Calabasas Historical Society event.\r\rPUBLIC HEARING\r\r CONTINUED PUBLIC HEARING - Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1012, approving a mitigated negative declaration; adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1013, approving GPA-004-003, PM-004-001, CUP-004-006, VAR-004-005 and OTP-005-009; and motion to waive further reading and introduction of Ordinance No. 2006-223, approving ZCH-004-005 for the subdivision of one parcel into two parcels, rough grading of one pad and driveway on one resulting parcel, and development of one single-family home including a pool/spa, horse stable/corral area, septic system, driveway, and retaining walls and dedication of 8.7 acres of permanent open space on the second resulting property located at 24135 Mulholland Highway (APN�s: 4455-006-012, -013).\r\r Mayor pro Tem Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer, to continue the public hearing to April 19, 2006. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1014, establishing revised affordable housing in-lieu fees for residential development projects and a revised affordable housing impact fee for commercial development projects, in accordance with Chapter 17.22 of the Municipal Code.\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015Mayor Washburn opened the public hearing.\r\r Tom Bartlett, Planning Manager, and consultants Karen Warner and Stanley Hoffman, presented the staff report. \r\rKathryn Palmer, Calabasas, spoke in opposition to staff�s recommendation and spoke in support of developers building affordable units. \r \r Mayor pro Tem Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to continue the public hearing to June 7, 2006. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\r The City Council recessed at 10:10 p.m. and reconvened at 10:20 p.m.\r\rNEW BUSINESS \r\r Discussion regarding the refunding of CFD 2001-1, Special Tax Assessment Bonds.\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson and Councilmember Groveman recused themselves and left the room. City Manager Coroalles recused himself from any discussion.\r\rGary Lysik, Chief Financial Officer, presented the staff report.\r\rMayor pro Tem Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer, to approve staff�s recommendation to pursue refunding of the Special Tax Assessment Bonds. MOTION CARRIED 3/0. Councilmember Wolfson and Councilmember Groveman were recused.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1015, amending Resolution Nos. 2002-770 and 2005-942 by adjusting the vacation leave accrual policy.\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson \u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer, to approve staff�s recommendation and adopt Resolution No. 2006-1015. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r\r Discussion regarding City Council meeting schedule changes.\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015The City Council approved moving the May 17, 2006 meeting to May 24, 2006 and moving the meetings of September 6 and 20, 2006 to September 13 and 27, 2006.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\r Presentation on City resurfacing program utilizing the Pavement Management System.\r\rNo Action Taken.\r\r Check Register for the period of February 23, 2006 to March 23, 2006.\r\rNo Action Taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS \r\r There were no task force reports.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT \r\r City Manager Coroalles indicated that he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS \r\r The City Council requested the following items:\r\rInventory of historical sites and development of historical preservation ordinance.\rOutline of issues regarding the equestrian use permit that was applied for the �farmhouse� property.\rInvestigate the City�s zoning ordinance regarding two horses vs. eight horses per acre.\rResolution in support of the Proposition 42 initiative.\r\rADJOURN \r\rThe City Council adjourned at 10:57 p.m.\r\r\r\r____________________________________ \rGwen Peirce, Assistant City Clerk\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 4 -\u0015\r04/05/2006\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 2 -\u0015\r04/05/2006\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u